## Patch-all + PTY activity

- Laptop **788× `coder ssh`** OOMed the operator machine. Do not do that.
- In-cluster one-process asyncio reconnecting-PTY loadgen on the **control** node (ClusterIP) is the right generator.
- Org-style patch: enqueue all stop then start into provisionerd (FIFO). Client `xargs -P 5` is not the org queue. Stops ran first, so “nothing running” until the stop drain finished.
- **771** patched running was the post-patch ceiling. **22** start builds **canceled**, **7 failed** (terraform), after unschedulable starts hung provisioners. UI “22 pending” was those **canceled** jobs; `coderd_provisionerd_jobs_current=0`. **10** k8s pods stayed Pending (`Too many pods`) as orphans.
- Under PTY: DERP p50 **0.92 ms** / p95 **4.8 ms** (n=655); agentstats median n=689, p50 **0.62 ms** / p95 **1.2 ms**. List over that window p50 **344 ms** / p95 **902 ms**. Loadgen never held 771 PTYs (~100 open, thousands of connect timeouts) and made the UI terminal unusable; Job was deleted.

